			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#875">SOTR Defection</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Hi Girls,<br />
<br />
As you may or may not know, a bunch of us have grown frustrated at the leadership (or lack thereof); of our current leader, and guild removed ourselves from SotR.<br />
<br />
This was a hard decision to make, and was made as a last resort. We wish there was another way, but there really wasn't.<br />
<br />
It was our original intent to just abandon the guild and move on. But after discussing and seeing all the un-appreciated work that Odeae, myself (and others) have done for SotR we decided to defect in favour of a fairer, more honest guild where we are not taken advantage of. One we have created ourselves. I hope Sisters who believe in us, follow us. And if you want to stay in SotR, thats fine, too.<br />
<br />
Please understand, this wasn't a power struggle, and is simply a matter of giving credit when credit is due, and showing respect for the hours of hard work we've given. We felt un-appreciated and used. While the details of the disagreements aren't important, basically it felt as if we were being taken advantage of, and had no real say in the guild. Odeae discussed this with the leader of SotR many times, but nothing changed. We found this unacceptable, and have created a guild where hopefully, something like this won't happen again.<br />
<br />
The new guild is pending, and has been approved by 10 people. It should be created in a few weeks. I hope all of you join &quot;Daughters of Artemis&quot; when it is created. In the meantime, feel free to stay in SotR if you like-- its not going anywhere and we're not trying to steal members from it. Any one who wishes to follow us to DoA, does so voluntarily. <br />
<br />
As for guildsay, I'm not entierly sure whats going to happen to this space. I may try and get it changed to 'DoA' once the guild goes live. You may have to all re-register, though. I'm not sure yet. I'm exceptionally sorry, but I didn't forsee this happening at all. In the meantime, since the guild-leader of SotR never bothered to register here, (although we asked her); we're still using this space as our temporary home, and now, DoA's home as well. <br />
<br />
If any current SotR members have questions about DoA, or don't understand whats happening--feel free to post in the forum.
						</td>
